Example: proceeds from a partial sale are a withdrawal from the selected fund.
On 2024-01-01, two FUND units were bought at 100 USD each; their closing value
of 200 USD becomes the opening value for the selected 2024-01-02 interval.
On 2024-01-02, one unit is sold for 130 USD (@ 130 USD), leaving one unit worth
140 USD at that day's quoted price. Only FUND is selected, so the sale contributes
-130 USD, while the remaining position has an ending value of 140 USD.
Profit/loss is 140 - 200 - (-130) = 70 USD. With the withdrawal treated as an
end-of-day flow, time-weighted return is (140 - (-130)) / 200 - 1 = 35%.
The money-weighted returns cannot be calculated for this one-day interval, so
the text formatter shows their null API values as n/a.

========== API ==========

investmentPerformance({ accounts: ['Assets:Fund'], commodities: ['FUND'], from: '2024-01-02', to: '2024-01-02' })

========== API FORMAT ==========

text

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
commodity FUND
  format 1,000 FUND
account Assets:Fund
account Assets:Cash
account Income:Gains
P 2024-01-01 FUND 100 USD
P 2024-01-02 FUND 140 USD

2024-01-01 Purchase
  Assets:Fund  2 FUND {100 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -200 USD

2024-01-02 Partial sale
  Assets:Fund  -1 FUND {100 USD} @ 130 USD
  Assets:Cash  130 USD
  Income:Gains  -30 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

Investment performance from 2024-01-02 to 2024-01-02
Instruments: 1
Opening value: 200.00 USD
Net contributions: -130.00 USD
Ending value: 140.00 USD
Profit/loss: 70.00 USD
Time-weighted return: 35.00 %
Money-weighted return (total): n/a
Money-weighted return (annualized): n/a

========== WARNINGS ==========
